### OrderQuery — Phase 2, Query Invocation (run-time)
### Calls a published Order query the way an independent client app would.
### Prereqs: order-query is running (./dry-run.sh) and orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch has been
### published with allowed_roles ["senior_DBA", "data-platform"] (run publish_query.http first,
### or publish it from the Query Builder UI).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Invoke the published query by its namespaced name, with a role allowed to call it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: senior_DBA

{
  "name": "orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED",
    "branchId": 12
  }
}

### Same call by bare name (an unambiguous short name also resolves), calling as a group that
### is in allowed_roles.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: data-platform

{
  "name": "ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": {
    "status": "QUEUED",
    "branchId": 12
  }
}

### 403 FORBIDDEN — chief_DBA exists in the catalog but isn't in this query's allowed_roles.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: chief_DBA

{
  "name": "orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED",
    "branchId": 12
  }
}

### 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT — missing a required param.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: senior_DBA

{
  "name": "orders.ordersByStatusAndBranch",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED"
  }
}

### 404 QUERY_NOT_FOUND — nothing published under this name.
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
X-Roles: senior_DBA

{
  "name": "orders.doesNotExist",
  "params": {
    "status": "SHIPPED",
    "branchId": 12
  }
}

### Sanity check: list published/drafted Order queries to see what's available to call.
POST {{baseUrl}}/engine/list
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Streaming. Needs the 50,000-row demo query (open the UI's "Downstream demo" page once, or draft,
### simulate and publish orders.historyByDate with fetchSize 100 and allowed role data-platform).
### Accept: application/x-ndjson streams one row per line, read from Postgres only as fast as the
### client reads. Without it, the same call returns 413 RESULT_TOO_LARGE (JSON is capped at 1000 rows).
POST {{baseUrl}}/data-query
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/x-ndjson
X-Roles: data-platform

{
  "name": "orders.historyByDate",
  "params": { "since": "2026-01-01" }
}
